# Line endings and encoding rules for this repository.
#
# Why this file exists:
#   This machine runs ANSI code page 936 (GBK), and Windows PowerShell 5.1
#   defaults Get-Content / Set-Content to -Encoding Default, which uses that
#   code page. Editing a UTF-8 file with Chinese text through those cmdlets
#   silently turns it into mojibake and writes the damage back. That already
#   destroyed MainWindow.xaml once and cost an afternoon.
#
#   The real guard is check-encoding.ps1 plus the .githooks/pre-commit hook,
#   which reject any commit containing U+FFFD, GBK mojibake, an odd number of
#   double quotes in a XAML line, or a UTF-8 BOM. This file handles the
#   line-ending half.
#
# Encoding note:
#   gitattributes cannot force the editor to write UTF-8. What it can do is
#   make the repository store a single canonical form, so a wrong encoding
#   shows up as an obvious diff instead of blending in.
#
# Line endings:
#   The whole tree is CRLF on disk (core.autocrlf=true). Declaring it here
#   keeps that stable across machines and checkouts.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

* text=auto eol=crlf

# Source and project files: CRLF, never treated as binary.
*.xaml        text eol=crlf
*.cs          text eol=crlf
*.csproj      text eol=crlf
*.sln         text eol=crlf
*.ps1         text eol=crlf
*.json        text eol=crlf
*.md          text eol=crlf
*.yml         text eol=crlf
*.yaml        text eol=crlf
.gitattributes text eol=crlf
.gitignore     text eol=crlf

# Git hooks must keep LF: sh chokes on CRLF in shebang scripts.
.githooks/*   text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch them.
*.dll   binary
*.exe   binary
*.pdb   binary
*.ico   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.zip   binary
*.nupkg binary
*.signature.p7s binary
